# Restart Flask after backend changes

After changing **backend** code in the `saptarishi` repo (Python under `backend/`, `data.json`, requirements, etc.):

1. Restart the Docker container named **`saptarishi_flask`** so the running API picks up the changes.
2. Prefer: `docker restart saptarishi_flask`
3. If restart fails, check status with `docker ps -a --filter name=saptarishi_flask` and report the error.
4. Do this in the same turn as the backend edit when practical — do not leave the user to restart manually.

Frontend-only changes in `ranjanravi.com` do **not** require restarting this container.
